{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784647881,"nonce":"SU0UCpcA4cWPL142MwPzyAoIyj8=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\nThe series list is DB-driven, and neither the rescan nor the TUI load\nreconciles a *terminal-state* series against the actual presence of its\n`b4/review/*` branch. So a thanked series whose branch was deleted on this\nmachine keeps its DB row — and its row is what the UI renders. This matches\nthe reporter's own confirmation: no local branch exists, yet the series\nshows, and deleting the review database makes it vanish.\n\n**1. `rescan_branches()` only marks *active* statuses gone.**\n`src/b4/review/tracking.py:2702-2714` — the full-rescan pass that flips a\nseries to `gone` when its branch is missing is gated to\n\n    active_statuses = ('reviewing', 'replied', 'partial', 'waiting')\n    ...\n    if s.get('status') in active_statuses and sid not in scanned_change_ids:\n        if not b4.git_branch_exists(topdir, branch_name):\n            update_series_status(conn, sid, 'gone', ...)\n\nA `thanked` (or `accepted` / `snoozed` / `queued`) series is outside that\ntuple, so a deleted branch never demotes it to `gone`. The reporter's\nseries were \"listed as thanked\" — exactly the excluded case.\n\n**2. `_load_series()` reconciles only the `new` → `reviewing` direction.**\n`src/b4/review_tui/_tracking_app.py:1019-1026` — the first pass has the full\nset of existing branches in hand (`existing_branches`, built once at\nline ~993) but uses it in one direction only:\n\n    if series.get('status') == 'new':\n        if branch_name in existing_branches:\n            series['status'] = 'reviewing'\n\nThere is no inverse check — a non-`new` series whose branch is *absent* from\n`existing_branches` is passed through untouched. The load also filters out\nonly `status == 'archived'` (line 978-979), so a `thanked` row survives the\nfilter and renders with its ✓ symbol.\n\n**3. The branch-existence check exists — but only on-demand.**\n`action_review` does verify the branch when the user tries to *reopen* a\nthanked series (`_tracking_app.py:1418-1421`, \"Review branch no longer\nexists; cannot reopen\"). That confirms the code knows how to detect the\ncondition; it just never runs it during list *display* or bulk update, so\nthe stale row stays visible until acted upon.\n\n## Why the sync workflow triggers it\n\nArchiving on the source machine both deletes the branch and moves the DB\nrow to `archived` (which `_load_series` hides). But the reporter synced some\nseries to the destination machine *before* archiving, so on the destination\nthe row is `thanked` (not `archived`) while the branch has since been\ndeleted. `thanked` + missing-branch is precisely the unreconciled\ncombination above → several hundred ghosts.\n\n## Related bugs\n\nSame review-TUI/DB-consistency family as the update path in `a0c4ddb`\n(this bug was split out from that investigation). Distinct from the\ndiscovery-side bugs. No fix suggestions per request.","files":null}]}